{"candidates":[{"content":"Relation Kind: Shared Mechanism (Retrospective Filtering via Error Elimination). The problem connects to the neighbourhood by asserting that both biological evolution and scientific theory selection operate via a shared mechanism of 'retrospective filtering,' where survival/corroboration is determined solely by past performance against severe tests, not future probability. Refuted If: It is demonstrated that scientific preference relies on a prospective normative element (e.g., an inductive expectation of future truth) that biological fitness fundamentally lacks, thereby breaking the mechanistic symmetry and reducing the relation to a mere metaphor rather than a structural identity.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"b3c0511b432396d0e2d2bf8490349317b336851e22777534cc85e5e6886fa5de"},{"role":"dependence","target":"8b7cece3d967663a5995c65918c732fb8f87d229ce749eeb590af5cc549a6337"},{"role":"dependence","target":"2b2849a64e01534a46cff6511f2c52e4711e7522bae536162e1f4e407ade0278"},{"role":"dependence","target":"003718cc784c1026759d441cbe548fb1375af2ed024df3ffdf107d0ed8bb0983"}],"typicality":0.85},{"content":"Relation Kind: Contradiction (Prospective Normativity vs. Retrospective Fitness). The problem stands in contradiction to the neighbourhood's evolutionary analogies by asserting that scientific preference inherently requires a prospective normative commitment (belief in future reliability) that biological evolution explicitly rejects as teleological. Refuted If: It is shown that scientists can and do prefer corroborated theories purely as strategic tools for error elimination without any underlying belief in their future truth or reliability, thereby aligning scientific preference perfectly with blind biological selection.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"461dc629214617dbaa5eef2d9a41102e3759a1e582b7aef13f1829d19fb0b561"},{"role":"dependence","target":"003718cc784c1026759d441cbe548fb1375af2ed024df3ffdf107d0ed8bb0983"}],"typicality":0.45},{"content":"Relation Kind: Abstraction (Error Elimination as Universal Operator). The problem abstracts the neighbourhood's specific cases into a universal operator 'E' (Error Elimination), where both biological mutation rejection and scientific falsification are instances of E applied to different domains (genotype vs. proposition). Refuted If: It is demonstrated that the 'cost' function in biological evolution (death/sterility) is ontologically distinct from the 'cost' in science (logical inconsistency/empirical mismatch) such that no single operator 'E' can describe both without losing explanatory power, rendering the abstraction empty.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"b3c0511b432396d0e2d2bf8490349317b336851e22777534cc85e5e6886fa5de"},{"role":"dependence","target":"461dc629214617dbaa5eef2d9a41102e3759a1e582b7aef13f1829d19fb0b561"},{"role":"dependence","target":"2b2849a64e01534a46cff6511f2c52e4711e7522bae536162e1f4e407ade0278"}],"typicality":0.6},{"content":"Relation Kind: Dependence (Scientific Preference Depends on Biological Analogy for Coherence). The problem asserts that the coherence of scientific preference (as non-inductive) is dependent on the biological analogy; without the model of blind variation and selective retention, the concept of 'corroboration without induction' collapses into irrationalism. Refuted If: It is shown that scientific preference can be fully grounded in logical pragmatism or social epistemology without any reference to biological evolution, proving the analogy is heuristic rather than foundational.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"8b7cece3d967663a5995c65918c732fb8f87d229ce749eeb590af5cc549a6337"},{"role":"dependence","target":"003718cc784c1026759d441cbe548fb1375af2ed024df3ffdf107d0ed8bb0983"}],"typicality":0.3},{"content":"Relation Kind: Integration (Hybrid Selection System). The problem proposes an integration relation where modern science is a hybrid system combining biological-style blind variation (creative conjecture) with a uniquely human normative filter (critical rationality), creating a new emergent mechanism distinct from both parents. Refuted If: It is demonstrated that 'critical rationality' is itself an evolved biological trait subject to the same blind selection pressures, meaning there is no second filter to integrate, only a single continuous evolutionary process.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"b3c0511b432396d0e2d2bf8490349317b336851e22777534cc85e5e6886fa5de"},{"role":"dependence","target":"461dc629214617dbaa5eef2d9a41102e3759a1e582b7aef13f1829d19fb0b561"},{"role":"dependence","target":"2b2849a64e01534a46cff6511f2c52e4711e7522bae536162e1f4e407ade0278"},{"role":"dependence","target":"003718cc784c1026759d441cbe548fb1375af2ed024df3ffdf107d0ed8bb0983"}],"typicality":0.55},{"content":"Relation Kind: Reduction (Science Reduces to Evolutionary Epistemology). The problem asserts a reduction relation where all norms of scientific preference are reducible to biological fitness conditions of the cognitive agent; 'rationality' is simply the name for cognitive strategies that enhanced ancestral survival. Refuted If: It is shown that scientific methods frequently prescribe actions (e.g., accepting counter-intuitive theories) that reduce individual biological fitness or reproductive success, proving that scientific norms cannot be reduced to biological imperatives.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"8b7cece3d967663a5995c65918c732fb8f87d229ce749eeb590af5cc549a6337"},{"role":"dependence","target":"2b2849a64e01534a46cff6511f2c52e4711e7522bae536162e1f4e407ade0278"},{"role":"dependence","target":"003718cc784c1026759d441cbe548fb1375af2ed024df3ffdf107d0ed8bb0983"}],"typicality":0.75}],"simulation_proposals":[]}